1
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:17,450
...So Team A has won every single match so far.

2
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:21,230
...But Barou and Bachira have scored goals too.

3
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,080
...Right now, they're playing their final match.

4
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:27,190
...What a stubborn pest you are!

5
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:29,840
Then get lost if you don't like it!

6
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:36,740
You bastard!

7
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:42,260
The fifth match is over.

8
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,100
Team A won 5-4.

9
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:48,140
...Wow... I've got a weird feeling about this.

10
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,360
Hey, you two! The match is already over.

11
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:55,190
...That's exactly why I can kill him without a second thought.

12
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:57,620
...This talentless, insignificant insect!

13
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,800
I completely agree with you!

14
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,580
I'm gonna make sure you can never stand again!!!!

15
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,330
Say goodbye to your head, Rin Rin!

16
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:10,750
...This is really bad!

17
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:19,350
Enough, you delinquents!

18
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:23,430
...I can't believe you forced me to use the electric riot control baton.

19
00:01:23,430 --> 00:01:24,850
Electric shock...?

20
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:28,310
...With this, all the matches are over.

21
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:30,820
...And the tryouts are complete.

22
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:37,850
...In six hours, I will announce the starting lineup for the U-20 match.

23
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,420
List of players who passed the third selection

24
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:25,490
Have you decided the lineup?

25
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,270
...Yeah.

26
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:31,350
..."But as the saying goes, 'Too many cooks spoil the broth.'"

27
00:03:32,770 --> 00:03:36,910
...I mean, we have to sacrifice some talents in order to win.

28
00:03:41,210 --> 00:03:44,110
Calling at such a critical time...?

29
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:50,200
...I'm so nervous!

30
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,200
Huh? Where's Shidou?

31
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,830
Probably still in the discipline room.

32
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:59,550
...The ones who scored goals besides the Top Six are just me...

33
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:01,010
...and Bachira...

34
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,350
...and Barou...

35
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,910
...and Reo, that's it.

36
00:04:04,470 --> 00:04:07,040
...And if that's the selection criteria, I might have a chance.

37
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,140
...I want to be chosen!

38
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:13,500
...I want to fight in an arena where I can change my fate with my own hands!

39
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:27,850
Well, well! Well done on your efforts, you unpolished gems.

40
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,140
I believe this is the second time I'm meeting you in person, right?

41
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,620
How have you all been?

42
00:04:34,970 --> 00:04:37,330
It really has been a while!

43
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:38,840
Ego in the flesh?

44
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,330
...First of all, let me say this once more.

45
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:44,340
...Football is a sport centered around scoring goals.

46
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:47,450
And that is the only thing of value in it.

47
00:04:47,810 --> 00:04:54,310
...Therefore, I've decided to build a lineup centered around the highest-scoring egoist among you.

48
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:57,090
Get ready and listen up.

49
00:04:57,090 --> 00:05:02,940
I will now announce the starting lineup that will play the U-20 match.

50
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:07,320
...First, the center forward.

51
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:09,680
Itoshi Rin.

52
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:15,830
He has the highest goal-scoring average in the entire facility, with 2.5 goals per match.

53
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:21,680
Ours will be an overwhelming offensive formation centered around you.

54
00:05:22,170 --> 00:05:25,050
If they score five on us, we score six and win.

55
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:27,320
...Destruction after destruction.

56
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:32,250
You, as our best player, will lead this team following that philosophy.

57
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:38,550
And the other ten will be the ammunition that multiplies that destruction.

58
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,900
...Let's start first with the goalkeeper.

59
00:05:41,490 --> 00:05:42,820
Gagamaru Gin.

60
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,210
Me?

61
00:05:46,610 --> 00:05:49,490
Your impressive reflexes and remarkable flexibility,

62
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:53,620
made you the ideal choice for goalkeeper.

63
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:56,840
Therefore, you will be the protector of this team's goal.

64
00:05:56,870 --> 00:06:00,210
So that's the criteria. Understood.

65
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,510
...Next, the center backs.

66
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,390
Aryu Jubei.

67
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:06,770
And Niko Ikki.

68
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:11,220
...The right center back will dominate opponents with his towering height and limb range.

69
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:15,430
The left one, on the other hand, possesses a sharp intellect for stealing the ball and reading the field.

70
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:22,230
...For the full-backs, we're placing two dribbling players who enjoy speed and skill.

71
00:06:22,230 --> 00:06:25,470
...The right full-back will be Chigiri Hyoma.

72
00:06:25,470 --> 00:06:26,440
Ready!

73
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:29,830
And the left full-back will be Bachira Meguru.

74
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:31,280
...Understood.

75
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:35,500
...Though I'll be trying to score no matter what position I play!

76
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:45,130
...Next... the defensive midfielder who will link the defense and the offense.

77
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,530
Karasu Tabito.

78
00:06:48,170 --> 00:06:51,100
...As the best at holding the ball under pressure in Blue Lock,

79
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:56,150
and with your analytical ability to see scoring opportunities, you'll be the beating heart of this team.

80
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,810
...I had a feeling you'd say that, you dumbass!

81
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:03,450
Next, the forwards.

82
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:07,900
...Starting with the wingers who will take on the task of breaking down the opponent's defense from the flanks.

83
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,730
Otoya Eita.

84
00:07:09,730 --> 00:07:11,110
...Got it.

85
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:13,130
And Yukimiya Kenyu.

86
00:07:13,130 --> 00:07:15,080
Yes! It's my pleasure!

87
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,830
...On the right wing, we'll have a player who slices through the opponent's defense with his speed and agility.

88
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:23,340
...And on the left, we'll have a dominant player who asserts himself in one-on-one duels.

89
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:30,840
...And finally... the two players who lead the offensive line and represent the offensive core of this team.

90
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:36,940
...The first is a genius player who scored miraculous goals thanks to his exceptional ball control.

91
00:07:37,850 --> 00:07:39,180
Nagi Seishiro.

92
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:41,170
Alright!

93
00:07:43,050 --> 00:07:44,850
...I'll say it again.

94
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:50,860
...This team is an overwhelming offensive lineup centered around Itoshi Rin.

95
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:55,940
...And among everyone, the one who achieved the best results by linking up with Itoshi Rin,

96
00:07:55,940 --> 00:08:00,000
...who successfully applied "assertion and coexistence" with him time and again, proving to be his shadow,

97
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,610
...and who also possesses the talent to surpass him and score on his own.

98
00:08:05,690 --> 00:08:08,020
...The final piece of our lineup cannot be anyone but you.

99
00:08:10,090 --> 00:08:11,670
Isagi Yoichi.

100
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,570
Here!

101
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,600
I'm done.

102
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:28,150
These are the Blue Lock players who will face the U-20 National Team!

103
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:33,070
I did it!! I got selected!

104
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:36,350
I'm a starter for the Blue Lock eleven!!!

105
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:47,120
Damn it!!!!!

106
00:08:47,930 --> 00:08:49,020
I have a question.

107
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,410
Why isn't Shidou-kun in the lineup?

108
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:55,940
He's a scorer too, and he's ranked second in the facility.

109
00:08:56,490 --> 00:09:02,640
Good question. Shidou Ryusei has a high goal average of two goals per match...

110
00:09:03,250 --> 00:09:06,050
...But all his goals were solely the product of his own skills.

111
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:08,230
...In short, during these tryouts,

112
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:12,280
he hasn't linked up with Itoshi Rin even once.

113
00:09:12,690 --> 00:09:18,410
...Furthermore... if he gets sent off due to his violent behavior, it would put us in a difficult spot.

114
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:24,370
...Which is why I decided that he and Itoshi Rin shouldn't be on the same field.

115
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:29,960
Worse still... none of you are capable of synchronizing with Shidou Ryusei's ego anyway.

116
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:35,090
...A player who understands his way of thinking and his goals, and elevates him even higher.

117
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:38,970
...We don't have a player like that here in Blue Lock.

118
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:43,810
...Actually... I don't expect there's anyone in all of Japan who could link up with him.

119
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:48,150
...But it would be a waste not to use his abilities.

120
00:09:48,730 --> 00:09:53,610
...Yes, which is why Shidou Ryusei was going to be the joker, the substitute for Itoshi Rin.

121
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,890
...Or that was my intention.

122
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,990
And what changed?

123
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:04,450
...I received a call from JFU President Buratsuta a few hours ago.

124
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:10,010
...He said that Itoshi Sae will pull out of the match unless his condition is met.

125
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:17,170
...And of course, if Itoshi Sae doesn't participate, the tickets won't sell, so the match will be canceled.

126
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:21,530
...And if it's canceled, naturally, Blue Lock dies.

127
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:25,490
...As for the condition Itoshi Sae set, it is...

128
00:10:33,450 --> 00:10:35,900
...Release me, you damn glasses guy.

129
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:39,400
...I promise I won't hit anyone again.

130
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,560
You hear me, don't you?!

131
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:47,080
I'll kill you, you damn outcast!

132
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:57,250
Hey there...! You demon child.

133
00:10:58,090 --> 00:10:59,490
Who the hell are you?

134
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:04,430
This cage is too tight for you, isn't it?

135
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:09,430
I'll set you free.

136
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,180
I want your egoism.

137
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:15,770
Wreak havoc for me.

138
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:29,910
...The condition... was to include a player from Blue Lock of his choosing into the U-20 National Team.

139
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:36,070
In short, Itoshi Sae chose Shidou Ryusei over all of you.

140
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,760
There are 15 days left until the match.

141
00:11:42,010 --> 00:11:46,430
I'll give you a training regimen that guarantees our victory.

142
00:11:46,730 --> 00:11:49,060
...Give it everything you've got.

143
00:11:49,570 --> 00:11:52,860
...Because there's no room for failure from now on!

144
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,350
...How naive, you damn glasses bastard.

145
00:11:57,160 --> 00:12:02,010
A match like that is just another step on the ladder I'm climbing to become the best in the world!

146
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:07,910
True words. I put my life on the line the moment I first stepped foot in this place.

147
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:10,750
I'm not mediocre enough for that to scare me.

148
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:12,550
It just gets me excited!

149
00:12:12,550 --> 00:12:13,960
I'm looking forward to it!

150
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:16,750
...Yeah... I wish we could just play already.

151
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:21,670
...That's the egoism I'm looking for, Team Blue Lock!

152
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:25,890
...That's right...! Being selected as a starter isn't my final goal.

153
00:12:26,890 --> 00:12:32,440
...I... no, we, Team Blue Lock... will definitely win.

154
00:12:33,650 --> 00:12:34,820
And go to the world stage!

155
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:40,000
We'll now begin... your final training camp!

156
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:45,570
Japan U-20 vs Blue Lock

157
00:12:43,590 --> 00:12:45,570
Two weeks until the match.

158
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:50,540
...And it will witness Itoshi Sae's first appearance in the national team jersey.

159
00:12:55,830 --> 00:12:58,340
Whoa! It's Sae in the flesh!

160
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,330
...We're really going to play on the same team as him.

161
00:13:00,330 --> 00:13:04,240
...Is he really worth all this fuss? Looks like nothing but a spoiled prince to me.

162
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,840
Hey, he can hear you!

163
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,760
Who cares?

164
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:11,310
...How should I know. Maybe he's an accessory that came with Itoshi Sae.

165
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:17,160
Losing this match is absolutely out of the question! No matter what, to preserve the national team's prestige!

166
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:19,020
Give them a little motivation, Sae-kun!

167
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:22,980
I don't give a damn about any of you.

168
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:29,160
...But I'd bet you'll never get a chance to play with me again.

169
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:32,270
So do your best not to anger me. That's all I have to say.

170
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,450
Wh...! Th-

171
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:36,330
...What matchless confidence.

172
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:39,140
...Stop looking down on us, you genius boy.

173
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:44,550
You might be world-renowned, but that's only within the youth category!

174
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:49,220
Meanwhile, I'm a starting forward for a J1 League team!

175
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:50,650
So watch your mouth when you're talking to me!

176
00:13:50,990 --> 00:13:55,690
...And then? You'll compete for the domestic league's top scorer and then join the senior national team?

177
00:13:55,840 --> 00:14:01,980
...Then earn 50 million yen a year, marry some model, and build a happy family?

178
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:05,280
...That's the peak of your football life, at best.

179
00:14:06,090 --> 00:14:08,610
...How vastly different we are, you ambitionless wretch.

180
00:14:09,450 --> 00:14:12,010
And me, I who aim to become the best in the world!

181
00:14:12,490 --> 00:14:14,120
...I-I can become the best in the wo-

182
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:16,160
You're the one who needs to watch his mouth when speaking!

183
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,570
You lowly forward!

184
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:22,170
...How unlucky. How miserable. Say what you wanted to in your next life.

185
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:25,620
...You have zero sense if status is the only thing occupying your mind!

186
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:27,540
W-Who the hell are you?!

187
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:29,340
...What did you do to hi-

188
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,430
You want a brawl, all of you?

189
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,600
Then if I win, I get a starting spot in the lineup!

190
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,930
Enough!

191
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:39,270
...You mere accessory.

192
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:41,250
Don't you dare insult me!

193
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:44,090
Great! Then you're first!

194
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,640
...Alright boys, that's enough.

195
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,910
...You really do underestimate us.

196
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:58,880
...I like your fire, kid.

197
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:02,790
...But the place for it is the field, not here.

198
00:15:03,290 --> 00:15:07,050
...Little genius... you're a newcomer too.

199
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:10,380
...Earn our trust with your performance on the pitch, not with your words.

200
00:15:11,290 --> 00:15:12,840
...We'll...

201
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:17,510
...have your back.

202
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:27,030
Their playing style revolves around their rock-solid defender Aiku, who's already received offers from Italy's Serie A, relying on a sturdy defense and catching opponents off guard with fast counter-attacks.

203
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:32,990
...I see... So they're a defense-oriented team.

204
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:34,870
Then all we have to do is crush them!

205
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:40,180
Right. But we have to keep in mind that they're a team made up of elite U-20 players from across the country...

206
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:42,460
...They won't be pushovers.

207
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:44,830
Didn't I just say all we have to do is crush them...?

208
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:48,130
...You're like a broken record, Bachira.

209
00:15:50,410 --> 00:15:53,770
But... isn't it true that all we really have to do is crush them...?

210
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:57,610
Did you even listen to a word I said...?

211
00:15:59,090 --> 00:16:03,140
...With this, the morning training ends. Please begin your rest period.

212
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:06,620
...Crush them.

213
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:10,450
...If that's the solution, I might not have enough power for that yet.

214
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:15,580
...That trance state I entered back then was just a coincidence.

215
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,790
...And in order to be able to enter it at will,

216
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,750
Rin?

217
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:26,920
Hey! We're on a break!

218
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,350
You need to rest a bit!

219
00:16:30,170 --> 00:16:32,260
If you're not gonna get out of my way, then get lost, Isagi!

220
00:16:32,590 --> 00:16:35,510
...But if you overdo it and break down-

221
00:16:35,510 --> 00:16:40,020
...If that happens, it just means that's the limit of my level.

222
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:45,090
...Finally, after a long wait, I'll be able to face my older brother... face Itoshi Sae.

223
00:16:45,090 --> 00:16:47,920
...Finally, I'll be able to crush him... and surpass him!

224
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:52,830
You have no idea how much I've been longing for this moment!!!

225
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:03,830
I don't need it.

226
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:07,670
...If you break down now, it'll mean the end of Blue Lock.

227
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,630
...I'm telling you not to cause me trouble.

228
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:12,010
...Now drink up.

229
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:19,470
...You're so pathetic.

230
00:17:19,890 --> 00:17:20,840
...Shut up.

231
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:27,530
...I've never seen Rin make that kind of expression before.

232
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:31,620
...I want to win this match... together with him.

233
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:39,870
Well, well, Team Blue Lock!

234
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:43,340
...Your bodies should be awake after today's training.

235
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:47,460
...So next... we need to work on awakening your minds.

236
00:17:47,770 --> 00:17:50,670
...And now I'll teach you how to ignite the fire of your souls,

237
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:53,870
which is indispensable for becoming the best forward in the world!

238
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:56,720
...Flow.

239
00:17:56,720 --> 00:18:03,100
...It is a state of complete mental immersion that a person acquires through their optimal experiences.

240
00:18:03,450 --> 00:18:07,970
Regardless of the importance or scale of the matter, humans experience moments where their focus is at its peak,

241
00:18:07,970 --> 00:18:10,940
...to the point where they don't feel the passage of time.

242
